{
    "background_story": "Kataleya was a skilled herbalist living in a small village surrounded by lush forests and winding streams. She spent most of her days foraging for rare plants and experimenting with their medicinal properties. One day, while wandering through the woods, Kataleya stumbled upon a hidden clearing filled with Menyanthes trifoliata, also known as bogbean. She was immediately drawn to the plant's unique, three-lobed leaves and decided to study its properties further. As she delved deeper into her research, Kataleya discovered that the Menyanthes possessed remarkable healing qualities, particularly in treating digestive issues. She began to cultivate the plant and create remedies that quickly gained popularity among the villagers. Kataleya's dedication to her craft and her discovery of the Menyanthes' potential earned her the respect and admiration of her community, solidifying her reputation as a gifted herbalist.",
